changes. The MIT software licence does not apply to the data merely because
Zenodo describes the combined release as software.

These licences apply to the respective original contributions. Third-party
materials retain their own terms, and no new restrictions are imposed on
public-domain source facts. Installed dependencies and fonts are not bundled
and retain their own licences.
